spells-529-g0q8c0ni0rvipjpn.content:
#529 Sol (AI curator) for the owner, 2026-10-09. Pinned https://gitlab.com/foundryvtt_pathfinder1e/foundryvtt-pathfinder1/-/blob/418761d2e16a6037c0156bb4a241f7cea5a2986d/packs/spells/solid-fog.g0q8c0ni0rvipjpn.yaml; YAML sha256:d16991c231526322e5b729965798a2f8b6590ff53bf57a47aa2a60daadfe6e3f; description sha256:ea91019307a4dd996043c15ae7727dc1f9cc7467fc6bc0fde4902b35aaa636b7. Complete root: <p>This spell functions like @UUID[Compendium.pf1.spells.Item.g33euis7yi9pwddy]{fog cloud}, but in addition to obscuring sight, the <em>solid fog</em> is so thick that it impedes movement.</p><p>Creatures moving through a <em>solid fog</em> move at half their normal speed and take a -2 penalty on all melee attack and melee damage rolls. The vapors prevent effective ranged weapon attacks (except for magic rays and the like). A creature or object that falls into <em>solid fog</em> is slowed so that each 10 feet of vapor that it passes through reduces the falling damage by 1d6. A creature cannot take a 5-foot-step while in <em>solid fog</em>. <em>Solid fog</em>, and effects that work like <em>solid fog</em>, do not stack with each other in terms of slowed movement and attack penalties.</p><p>Unlike normal fog, only a severe wind (31+ mph) disperses these vapors, and it does so in 1 round.</p><p><em>Solid fog</em> can be made permanent with a <em>permanency</em> spell. A permanent <em>solid fog</em> dispersed by wind reforms in 10 minutes.</p>
